Bundled color schemes
======================

ocode bundles the following community color schemes. ocode uses only the
foreground (syntax) colors from each; the background defined by a theme is never
applied, so your terminal's own background is preserved.

Each scheme is distributed under the MIT License by its respective author.
ocode redistributes the unmodified .tmTheme files; copyright remains with the
original authors.

  Dracula          https://github.com/dracula/sublime
  One Dark         https://github.com/andresmichel/one-dark-theme
  One Half Dark    https://github.com/sonph/onehalf
  One Half Light   https://github.com/sonph/onehalf
  Coldark Dark     https://github.com/armandphilippot/coldark-bat
  Coldark Cold     https://github.com/armandphilippot/coldark-bat
  Sublime Snazzy   https://github.com/greggb/sublime-snazzy
  Two Dark         https://github.com/erremauro/TwoDark

The seven base16 / Solarized / GitHub schemes that ship by default come from the
syntect library (https://github.com/trishume/syntect, MIT).

To add your own: drop any .tmTheme file into  ~/.config/ocode/themes/
(or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocode/themes/). It is loaded automatically at startup.
